IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law (8 Del. C. ch. 1), section 220(a) and (b): inspection of books and records; the
-- definitions, and the stockholder's right and its conditions. Layer 1, from the text alone. Quote lines are copied from
-- de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt by script. The Court's powers and the burdens of proof ((c) to (h)) are in
-- dg4-s220-court-orders.l4.
--
-- Section 220 is not on the lists of s 114(b) or (c), so it applies to a nonstock corporation with members for stockholders;
-- (b)(5) says so in words ("or a member of a nonstock corporation"). See `s 220(a)(3)` and the fork F-M in NOTES.md.

§ `s 220 Inspection of books and records`

§§ `s 220(a)(1) "Books and records"`

-- "Books and records" means: a. the certificate of incorporation (as defined in s 104) with agreements or instruments
-- incorporated by reference; b. the bylaws then in effect, likewise; c. minutes of all meetings of stockholders and the signed
-- consents evidencing action by stockholders without a meeting, for the 3 years preceding the date of the demand; d. all
-- communications in writing or by electronic transmission to stockholders generally within the past 3 years preceding the date of
-- the demand; e. minutes of any meeting of the board or a committee and records of any action of the board or a committee; f.
-- materials provided to the board or a committee in connection with its actions; g. annual financial statements of the
-- corporation for the 3 years preceding the date of the demand; h. any agreement entered into under s 122(18); i. director and
-- officer independence questionnaires.
-- src:843 | (1) “Books and records” means all of the following:
-- src:844 | a. The “certificate of incorporation,” as defined in § 104 of this title, including a copy of any agreement or other instrument incorporated by reference in the certificate of incorporation.
-- src:845 | b. The bylaws then in effect, including a copy of any agreement or other instrument incorporated by reference in the bylaws.
-- src:846 | c. Minutes of all meetings of stockholders and the signed consents evidencing all action taken by stockholders without a meeting, in each case for the 3 years preceding the date of the demand under subsection (b) of this section.
-- src:847 | d. All communications in writing or by electronic transmission to stockholders generally within the past 3 years preceding the date of the demand under subsection (b) of this section.
-- src:848 | e. Minutes of any meeting of the board of directors or any committee of the board of directors and records of any action of the board of directors or any such committee.
-- src:849 | f. Materials provided to the board of directors or any committee of the board of directors in connection with actions taken by the board of directors or any such committee.
-- src:850 | g. Annual financial statements of the corporation for the 3 years preceding the date of the demand under subsection (b) of this section.
-- src:851 | h. Any agreement entered into under § 122(18) of this title.
-- src:852 | i. Director and officer independence questionnaires.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(a)(1) (src:843-852)
DECLARE `s 220(a)(1) Kind of record` IS ONE OF
    `the certificate of incorporation, with any agreement or other instrument incorporated by reference in it` -- out of range: s 104, "certificate of incorporation" as defined (piece dg1)
    `the bylaws then in effect, with any agreement or other instrument incorporated by reference in them`
    `minutes of meetings of stockholders and signed consents evidencing action taken by stockholders without a meeting`
    `communications in writing or by electronic transmission to stockholders generally`
    `minutes of a meeting of the board of directors or a committee and records of an action of the board or a committee`
    `materials provided to the board of directors or a committee in connection with actions taken by it`
    `annual financial statements of the corporation`
    `an agreement entered into under s 122(18)` -- out of range: s 122(18) (piece dg2)
    `a director and officer independence questionnaire`
    `any other record of the corporation`

-- The three kinds bounded in time are bounded by the 3 years preceding the date of the demand. The record's date is the date
-- of the meeting or consent, of the communication, or the end of the year the financial statements are for (fork F-3Y).
-- The window runs from the demand date less 3 years (that day counts) to the demand date. A record that is not among the nine
-- kinds is not "books and records" (it may still be a record a director, a court or another law reaches).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(a)(1) (src:843-852)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 220(a)(1) Kind of record`
      `the date of the record` IS A DATE
      `the date of the demand` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 220(a)(1) the record is among the books and records` kind `the date of the record` `the date of the demand` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `minutes of meetings of stockholders and signed consents evidencing action taken by stockholders without a meeting` THEN `the date of the record is within the 3 years preceding the date of the demand`
    WHEN `communications in writing or by electronic transmission to stockholders generally` THEN `the date of the record is within the 3 years preceding the date of the demand`
    WHEN `annual financial statements of the corporation` THEN `the date of the record is within the 3 years preceding the date of the demand`
    WHEN `any other record of the corporation` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE
    WHERE
        `the date of the record is within the 3 years preceding the date of the demand` MEANS
                `the date of the record` AT LEAST (`the date` (`period in years` 3) `before` `the date of the demand`)
            AND `the date of the record` AT MOST `the date of the demand`

§§ `s 220(a)(2) to (5) The other definitions`

-- "Proper purpose" means a purpose reasonably related to a stockholder's interest as a stockholder. Whether it is so related is a
-- judgment (ultimately the Court's), taken as a fact.
-- src:853 | (2) “Proper purpose” means a purpose reasonably related to a stockholder’s interest as a stockholder.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(a)(2) (src:853)
GIVEN `the purpose is reasonably related to the stockholder's interest as a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 220(a)(2) the purpose is a proper purpose` `the purpose is reasonably related to the stockholder's interest as a stockholder` MEANS
    `the purpose is reasonably related to the stockholder's interest as a stockholder`

-- "Stockholder" means a person who is a holder of record of stock in a stock corporation, or a person who is the beneficial owner
-- of shares of such stock held either in a voting trust or by a nominee on behalf of that person. For a nonstock corporation, s
-- 114(a) reads "stockholder" as member, and (b)(5) names "a member of a nonstock corporation" (fork F-M).
-- src:854 | (3) “Stockholder” means a person who is a holder of record of stock in a stock corporation, or a person who is the beneficial owner of shares of such stock held either in a voting trust or by a nominee on behalf of such person.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(a)(3) (src:854); § 220(b)(5) (src:872)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of corporation`
      `the person is a holder of record of stock in the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the beneficial owner of shares of such stock held in a voting trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the beneficial owner of shares of such stock held by a nominee on behalf of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 220(a)(3) the person is a stockholder for the purposes of this section` kind `the person is a holder of record of stock in the corporation` `the person is the beneficial owner of shares of such stock held in a voting trust` `the person is the beneficial owner of shares of such stock held by a nominee on behalf of the person` `the person is a member of the corporation` MEANS
    IF `the kind is a stock corporation` kind
    THEN    `the person is a holder of record of stock in the corporation`
         OR `the person is the beneficial owner of shares of such stock held in a voting trust`
         OR `the person is the beneficial owner of shares of such stock held by a nominee on behalf of the person`
    ELSE `the person is a member of the corporation`

-- "Subsidiary" means any entity directly or indirectly owned, in whole or in part, by the corporation of which the stockholder is a
-- stockholder and over the affairs of which the corporation directly or indirectly exercises control, and includes, without
-- limitation, corporations, partnerships, limited partnerships, limited liability partnerships, limited liability companies,
-- statutory trusts and/or joint ventures. The kind of entity does not matter.
-- src:855 | (4) “Subsidiary” means any entity directly or indirectly owned, in whole or in part, by the corporation of which the stockholder is a stockholder and over the affairs of which the corporation directly or indirectly exercises control, and includes, without limitation, corporations, partnerships, limited partnerships, limited liability partnerships, limited liability companies, statutory trusts and/or joint ventures.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(a)(4) (src:855)
GIVEN `the entity is directly or indirectly owned, in whole or in part, by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation directly or indirectly exercises control over the affairs of the entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 220(a)(4) the entity is a subsidiary` `the entity is directly or indirectly owned, in whole or in part, by the corporation` `the corporation directly or indirectly exercises control over the affairs of the entity` MEANS
        `the entity is directly or indirectly owned, in whole or in part, by the corporation`
    AND `the corporation directly or indirectly exercises control over the affairs of the entity`

-- "Under oath" includes statements the declarant affirms to be true under penalty of perjury under the laws of the United States
-- or any state.
-- src:856 | (5) “Under oath” includes statements the declarant affirms to be true under penalty of perjury under the laws of the United States or any state.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(a)(5) (src:856)
GIVEN `the statement is made under oath in the ordinary sense` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declarant affirms the statement to be true under penalty of perjury under the laws of the United States or any state` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 220(a)(5) the statement is under oath` `the statement is made under oath in the ordinary sense` `the declarant affirms the statement to be true under penalty of perjury under the laws of the United States or any state` MEANS
        `the statement is made under oath in the ordinary sense`
    OR  `the declarant affirms the statement to be true under penalty of perjury under the laws of the United States or any state`

§§ `s 220(b)(5) to (7) The form and manner of the demand`

-- (5) Where the stockholder is other than a record holder of stock in a stock corporation or a member of a nonstock corporation,
-- the demand under oath shall state the person's status as a stockholder, be accompanied by documentary evidence of beneficial
-- ownership of the stock, and state that the documentary evidence is a true and correct copy of what it purports to be.
-- (6) Where an attorney or other agent seeks the inspection, the demand under oath shall be accompanied by a power of attorney or
-- other writing authorizing the attorney or agent to act for the stockholder.
-- (7) The demand under oath shall be directed to the corporation at its registered office in this State or at its principal
-- place of business.
-- That the demand be in writing and under oath comes from (b)(1). Together these are "the form and manner of making demand"
-- that (c)(2) speaks of.
-- src:872 | (5) In every instance where the stockholder is other than a record holder of stock in a stock corporation, or a member of a nonstock corporation, the demand under oath shall state the person’s status as a stockholder, be accompanied by documentary evidence of beneficial ownership of the stock, and state that such documentary evidence is a true and correct copy of what it purports to be.
-- src:873 | (6) In every instance where an attorney or other agent shall be the person who seeks the right to inspection, the demand under oath shall be accompanied by a power of attorney or such other writing which authorizes the attorney or other agent to so act on behalf of the stockholder.
-- src:874 | (7) The demand under oath shall be directed to the corporation at its registered office in this State or at its principal place of business.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(b)(5) (src:872); § 220(b)(6) (src:873); § 220(b)(7) (src:874)
DECLARE `s 220(b) Demand` HAS
    `the demand is in writing`                                                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the demand is under oath`                                                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is other than a record holder of stock in a stock corporation or a member of a nonstock corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the demand states the person's status as a stockholder`                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the demand is accompanied by documentary evidence of beneficial ownership of the stock`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the demand states that the documentary evidence is a true and correct copy of what it purports to be`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `an attorney or other agent seeks the inspection`                                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the demand is accompanied by a power of attorney or other writing authorizing the attorney or agent`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the demand is directed to the corporation at its registered office in this State or at its principal place of business` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(b)(1) (src:857); § 220(b)(5) (src:872); § 220(b)(6) (src:873); § 220(b)(7) (src:874)
GIVEN demand IS A `s 220(b) Demand`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 220(b) the demand complies with this section respecting the form and manner of making demand` demand MEANS
        demand's `the demand is in writing`
    AND demand's `the demand is under oath`
    AND (   (NOT demand's `the person is other than a record holder of stock in a stock corporation or a member of a nonstock corporation`)
         OR (    demand's `the demand states the person's status as a stockholder`
             AND demand's `the demand is accompanied by documentary evidence of beneficial ownership of the stock`
             AND demand's `the demand states that the documentary evidence is a true and correct copy of what it purports to be`))
    AND (   (NOT demand's `an attorney or other agent seeks the inspection`)
         OR demand's `the demand is accompanied by a power of attorney or other writing authorizing the attorney or agent`)
    AND demand's `the demand is directed to the corporation at its registered office in this State or at its principal place of business`

§§ `s 220(b)(2) The conditions on inspecting the corporation's books and records`

-- A stockholder may inspect and copy the corporation's books and records only if all of the following apply: a. the demand is
-- made in good faith and for a proper purpose; b. it describes with reasonable particularity the purpose and the books and
-- records sought; c. the books and records sought are specifically related to the purpose.
-- src:864 | (2) A stockholder may inspect and copy the corporation’s books and records only if all of the following apply:
-- src:865 | a. The stockholder’s demand is made in good faith and for a proper purpose.
-- src:866 | b. The stockholder’s demand describes with reasonable particularity the stockholder’s purpose and the books and records the stockholder seeks to inspect.
-- src:867 | c. The books and records sought are specifically related to the stockholder’s purpose.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(b)(2) (src:864-867)
GIVEN `the demand is made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is a proper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the demand describes the purpose with reasonable particularity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the demand describes the books and records sought with reasonable particularity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the books and records sought are specifically related to the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 220(b)(2) the conditions for inspecting and copying the corporation's books and records are met` `the demand is made in good faith` `the purpose is a proper purpose` `the demand describes the purpose with reasonable particularity` `the demand describes the books and records sought with reasonable particularity` `the books and records sought are specifically related to the purpose` MEANS
        `the demand is made in good faith`
    AND `the purpose is a proper purpose`
    AND `the demand describes the purpose with reasonable particularity`
    AND `the demand describes the books and records sought with reasonable particularity`
    AND `the books and records sought are specifically related to the purpose`

§§ `s 220(b)(1) The right to inspect`

-- Subject to (b)(2), any stockholder, in person or by attorney or other agent, shall, upon written demand under oath, have the
-- right during the usual hours for business to inspect for any proper purpose, and to make copies and extracts from, a. the
-- corporation's stock ledger, a list of its stockholders, and its other books and records; and b. a subsidiary's books and
-- records, to the extent that (1) the corporation has actual possession and control of them, or (2) the corporation could obtain
-- them through the exercise of control over the subsidiary, provided that as of the date of the demand A. inspection would not
-- breach an agreement between the corporation or the subsidiary and a person or persons not affiliated with the corporation, and
-- B. the subsidiary would not have the right under the law applicable to it to deny the corporation access on demand.
-- The stock ledger and the list of stockholders are not among the "books and records" that (b)(2) restricts, so for them the
-- right needs a stockholder, a demand in the required form and manner, and a proper purpose; for the books and records the
-- conditions of (b)(2) and the definition in (a)(1) apply as well.
-- src:857 | (b) (1) Subject to paragraph (b)(2) of this section, any stockholder, in person or by attorney or other agent, shall, upon written demand under oath, have the right during the usual hours for business to inspect for any proper purpose, and to make copies and extracts from:
-- src:858 | a. The corporation’s stock ledger, a list of its stockholders, and its other books and records; and
-- src:859 | b. A subsidiary’s books and records, to the extent that:
-- src:860 | 1. The corporation has actual possession and control of such records of such subsidiary; or
-- src:861 | 2. The corporation could obtain such records through the exercise of control over such subsidiary, provided that as of the date of the making of the demand:
-- src:862 | A. The stockholder inspection of such books and records of the subsidiary would not constitute a breach of an agreement between the corporation or the subsidiary and a person or persons not affiliated with the corporation; and
-- src:863 | B. The subsidiary would not have the right under the law applicable to it to deny the corporation access to such books and records upon demand by the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(b)(1) (src:857-863)
GIVEN `the person is a stockholder for the purposes of this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the demand complies with this section respecting the form and manner of making demand` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is a proper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 220(b)(1)a. the stockholder has the right to inspect and copy the stock ledger and the list of stockholders` `the person is a stockholder for the purposes of this section` `the demand complies with this section respecting the form and manner of making demand` `the purpose is a proper purpose` MEANS
        `the person is a stockholder for the purposes of this section`
    AND `the demand complies with this section respecting the form and manner of making demand`
    AND `the purpose is a proper purpose`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(b)(1) (src:857-863); § 220(b)(2) (src:864-867)
GIVEN `the person is a stockholder for the purposes of this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the demand complies with this section respecting the form and manner of making demand` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions for inspecting and copying the corporation's books and records are met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the record is among the books and records` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 220(b)(1)a. the stockholder has the right to inspect and copy the corporation's books and records` `the person is a stockholder for the purposes of this section` `the demand complies with this section respecting the form and manner of making demand` `the conditions for inspecting and copying the corporation's books and records are met` `the record is among the books and records` MEANS
        `the person is a stockholder for the purposes of this section`
    AND `the demand complies with this section respecting the form and manner of making demand`
    AND `the conditions for inspecting and copying the corporation's books and records are met`
    AND `the record is among the books and records`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(b)(1) (src:859-863)
GIVEN `the stockholder has the right to inspect and copy the corporation's books and records` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has actual possession and control of the subsidiary's records` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation could obtain the subsidiary's records through the exercise of control over the subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `as of the date of the demand, inspection would not constitute a breach of an agreement between the corporation or the subsidiary and a person not affiliated with the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `as of the date of the demand, the subsidiary would not have the right under the law applicable to it to deny the corporation access on demand` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 220(b)(1)b. the stockholder has the right to inspect and copy the subsidiary's books and records` `the stockholder has the right to inspect and copy the corporation's books and records` `the corporation has actual possession and control of the subsidiary's records` `the corporation could obtain the subsidiary's records through the exercise of control over the subsidiary` `as of the date of the demand, inspection would not constitute a breach of an agreement between the corporation or the subsidiary and a person not affiliated with the corporation` `as of the date of the demand, the subsidiary would not have the right under the law applicable to it to deny the corporation access on demand` MEANS
        `the stockholder has the right to inspect and copy the corporation's books and records`
    AND (   `the corporation has actual possession and control of the subsidiary's records`
         OR (    `the corporation could obtain the subsidiary's records through the exercise of control over the subsidiary`
             AND `as of the date of the demand, inspection would not constitute a breach of an agreement between the corporation or the subsidiary and a person not affiliated with the corporation`
             AND `as of the date of the demand, the subsidiary would not have the right under the law applicable to it to deny the corporation access on demand`))

§§ `s 220(b)(3) What the corporation may impose, and redact`

-- The corporation may impose reasonable restrictions on the confidentiality, use, or distribution of books and records and may
-- require, as a condition to producing books and records to a stockholder under any demand under this subsection, that the
-- stockholder agree that any information included in the books and records is deemed incorporated by reference in any complaint
-- filed by or at the direction of the stockholder in relation to the subject matter referenced in the demand. The corporation
-- may redact portions of any books and records produced to the extent the portions redacted are not specifically related to the
-- stockholder's purpose.
-- src:868 | (3) The corporation may impose reasonable restrictions on the confidentiality, use, or distribution of books and records and may require, as a condition to producing books and records to a stockholder under any demand under this subsection, that the stockholder agree that any information included in the corporation’s books and records is deemed incorporated by reference in any complaint filed by or at the direction of the stockholder in relation to the subject matter referenced in the demand. The corporation may redact portions of any books and records produced to such stockholder under this subsection to the extent the portions so redacted are not specifically related to the stockholder’s purpose.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(b)(3) (src:868)
DECLARE `s 220(b)(3) What the corporation may impose or do` IS ONE OF
    `impose reasonable restrictions on the confidentiality, use or distribution of books and records`
    `require, as a condition to producing books and records, that the stockholder agree that any information in them is deemed incorporated by reference in any complaint filed by or at the direction of the stockholder in relation to the subject matter referenced in the demand`
    `redact a portion of the books and records produced`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(b)(3) (src:868)
GIVEN measure IS A `s 220(b)(3) What the corporation may impose or do`
      `a demand has been made under subsection (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the portion is specifically related to the stockholder's purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 220(b)(3) the corporation may do it` measure `a demand has been made under subsection (b)` `the portion is specifically related to the stockholder's purpose` MEANS
        `a demand has been made under subsection (b)`
    AND CONSIDER measure
        WHEN `impose reasonable restrictions on the confidentiality, use or distribution of books and records` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `require, as a condition to producing books and records, that the stockholder agree that any information in them is deemed incorporated by reference in any complaint filed by or at the direction of the stockholder in relation to the subject matter referenced in the demand` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `redact a portion of the books and records produced` THEN NOT `the portion is specifically related to the stockholder's purpose`

§§ `s 220(b)(4) What the section does not affect`

-- This section does not affect a. the right of a stockholder to seek discovery of books and records if the stockholder is in
-- litigation with the corporation, to the same extent as any other litigant; or b. the power of a court, independently of this
-- chapter, to compel the production of corporate records for inspection and to impose reasonable restrictions as provided in
-- (b)(3), provided that, in the case of production of "books and records" at the request of a stockholder, the stockholder has met
-- the requirements of this subsection.
-- src:869 | (4) This section does not affect:
-- src:870 | a. The right of a stockholder to seek discovery of books and records if the stockholder is in litigation with the corporation, to the same extent as any other litigant; or
-- src:871 | b. The power of a court, independently of this chapter, to compel the production of corporate records for inspection and to impose reasonable restrictions as provided in paragraph (b)(3) of this section, provided that, in the case of production of “books and records” defined in subsection (a) of this section at the request of a stockholder, the stockholder has met the requirements of this subsection.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(b)(4) (src:869-871)
GIVEN `the stockholder is in litigation with the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 220(b)(4)a. this section affects the stockholder's right to seek discovery of books and records from the corporation as any other litigant may` `the stockholder is in litigation with the corporation` MEANS
    IF `the stockholder is in litigation with the corporation`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(b)(4) (src:871)
GIVEN `the production is of books and records defined in subsection (a), at the request of a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stockholder has met the requirements of subsection (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 220(b)(4)b. the power of a court independently of this chapter to compel production of corporate records for inspection may be exercised` `the production is of books and records defined in subsection (a), at the request of a stockholder` `the stockholder has met the requirements of subsection (b)` MEANS
        (NOT `the production is of books and records defined in subsection (a), at the request of a stockholder`)
    OR  `the stockholder has met the requirements of subsection (b)`
